{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsrcs=[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S45-transconf-block\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"epaxos/exec.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":83,\\\"end_line\\\":91,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"S46-transconf-doc\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"epaxos/epaxos.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":31,\\\"end_line\\\":38,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"S47-run-transconf\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"run.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":233,\\\"end_line\\\":237,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}]\nclaim={\\\"id\\\":\\\"C12-transitive-skip-executes-commuting-command\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"concern\\\":\\\"implementation_semantics\\\",\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"When transitive-conflict skipping is enabled, executing an instance must not wait for a prior command it commutes with: the executor's transitive-conflict branch must let the commuting dependency be skipped instead of halting on it.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S45-transconf-block\\\",\\\"S46-transconf-doc\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"One replica with the transconf flag set: a committed instance whose command touches one key and whose only dependency is an uncommitted command on a different key, both reachable by the executor.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"the flag is the switch the implementation provides for this behaviour\\\",\\\"the two commands commute under the state package's conflict relation\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"the launched configuration, which passes transconf=false\\\",\\\"whether skipping such a dependency is sound in general\\\",\\\"the rest of the executor's closure computation\\\"]},\n \\\"pending\\\":[],\n \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S45-transconf-block\\\",\\\"S46-transconf-doc\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB13-transconf\\\"],\n  \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The implementation documents transitive-conflict skipping as one of its differences from the original code base, and the executor contains a branch gated on the flag that inspects every pair of commands and takes no action when none of them conflict; the flag therefore changes nothing while the documented behaviour would let a commuting prior command be skipped.\\\",\n  \\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Applies whenever a caller enables the flag through epaxos.New; the shipped launcher passes false, so the default deployment is unaffected.\\\",\n  \\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"whether the branch was intended to prune the dependency from the closure, which the empty body suggests but no comment states\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}}\nb13={\\\"id\\\":\\\"BB13-transconf\\\",\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"S45-transconf-block\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"TransitiveConflictBlock\\\":\\\"strongconnect\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":83,\\\"end_line\\\":91}\nb13={\\\"id\\\":\\\"BB13-transconf\\\",\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"S45-transconf-block\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"strongconnect\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":58,\\\"end_line\\\":149,\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Tarjan closure over an instance's dependencies, including the flag-gated transitive-conflict branch that inspects command pairs and takes no action.\\\",\n \\\"associations\\\":[{\\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C12-transitive-skip-executes-commuting-command\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S45-transconf-block\\\",\\\"S46-transconf-doc\\\"],\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The branch is where the documented skipping would happen; as written it only computes conflicts, so the dependency that would be skipped is still waited on.\\\"}],\n \\\"pending\\\":[]}\nplan={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: with the transitive-skip flag on, does executing a committed instance whose command commutes with its uncommitted dependency succeed, or does it wait for that dependency as if the flag were off? Prefix: the harness builds the two records with the package's own constructors and calls the executor's entry for the committed instance. Controls: the prerequisite prints the flag, both statuses and that the two commands commute, and the result prints whether execution happened and the statuses afterwards.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":claim[\\\"id\\\"],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB13-transconf\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test that prepares a commuting uncommitted dependency and asks the real executor to run the committed instance with the flag set.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"harness-only scaffolding: the Replica is constructed in-package with the flag set and the two records are built directly with the package's types\\\",\\\"the harness calls the executor entry directly instead of the execution loop\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"transconf_case\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"transconf_prepared\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"transconf\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"commands_commute\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]}],\n  \\\"legality\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S45-transconf-block\\\",\\\"S46-transconf-doc\\\",\\\"S47-run-transconf\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB13-transconf\\\"],\n   \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The flag is set exactly as a caller would through epaxos.New, and the records are the states a replica reaches (one committed with a dependency on one uncommitted instance).\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"One replica, two records, flag on.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"the soundness of skipping is out of scope\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-transconf\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-transconf\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"transconf_execution\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB13-transconf\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S45-transconf-block\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB13-transconf\\\"],\n    \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event reports whether the executor ran the instance and the statuses afterwards, which is the observable of the documented skipping.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The flag was on and the commands commute.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"dependency_status\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"transconf_case.dependency_status\\\"}],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"transconf_case\\\"}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-transconf\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"transconf_execution\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"executed\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"dependency_status\\\"],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"With transitive-conflict skipping enabled, execution must not wait for a prior command it commutes with.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"the check does not establish whether skipping is sound in general, only whether the documented behaviour occurs\\\",\\\"the flag is false in the shipped configuration\\\"]}\nq={\\\"audit_spec_version\\\":17,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"ready_for_check\\\",\\\"preferred_check\\\":\\\"direct_test\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"With the transitive-skip flag enabled, a committed instance whose command commutes with its only dependency (an uncommitted command on another key) is given to the executor. Does execution proceed by skipping that commuting dependency, or does it wait for it exactly as if the flag were off?\\\",\n \\\"importance\\\":\\\"The implementation documents transitive-conflict skipping as one of its differences from the original code base, and a caller can enable it through the constructor, yet if execution still waits then the flag buys nothing and the documented optimization is inert. The consequence is performance rather than safety, and the shipped configuration sets the flag false, so the finding is bounded to callers that enable it.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S45-transconf-block\\\",\\\"S46-transconf-doc\\\",\\\"S47-run-transconf\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\",\\\"S20-exec\\\",\\\"S21-quorum-sizes\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\"],\n \\\"contexts\\\":[\\\"transconf enabled through the constructor\\\",\\\"committed instance with a commuting uncommitted dependency\\\"],\n \\\"event_paths\\\":[\\\"the executor walks the committed instance's dependencies\\\",\\\"the flag-gated branch inspects command pairs\\\",\\\"execution either proceeds or halts on the uncommitted dependency\\\"],\n \\\"activity_classes\\\":[\\\"A5\\\"],\\\"behavior_ids\\\":[\\\"B8-scc-closure\\\"],\\\"fact_ids\\\":[\\\"F3-execution-prefix\\\"],\n \\\"supporting_behavior_ids\\\":{\\\"B7-execute-scheduler\\\":\\\"the scheduler that calls the closure computation\\\",\\\"B6-commit-install\\\":\\\"how the two records reach their statuses\\\"},\n \\\"obligation_relation_kind\\\":\\\"consumption\\\",\\\"priority\\\":1,\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"scoped to the source: the flag-gated branch inspects every command pair and takes no action, so nothing in the executor changes when the flag is set (S45-transconf-block, S46-transconf-doc)\\\",\n   \\\"scoped to the run: the local construction run with the flag on reports executed false while the two commands commute (transconf_prepared commands_commute true, transconf_execution executed false)\\\",\n   \\\"scoped to the configuration: run.go passes transconf false, so the launched deployment never sets the flag (S47-run-transconf)\\\"],\n \\\"unknowns\\\":[\\\"whether the intended pruning was to drop the dependency from the closure or to relax the ready check, which the empty body leaves open\\\"],\n \\\"trigger_rationale\\\":\\\"The principal fact is the execution prefix the executor advances (F3): with the flag on, the documented behaviour would let it advance past a commuting prior command, while the observed behaviour leaves the row stopped. The activity is consumption (A5), where the committed decision's commands are applied.\\\"}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"New obligation and its first check for the last recorded discrepancy: the executor's transitive-conflict branch, which the implementation documents as skipping prior commuting commands, only inspects command pairs and takes no action. The harness builds exactly the documented situation with the flag on - a committed instance whose command commutes with its uncommitted dependency - and the local construction run shows execution halting (executed false) as if the flag were off. The finding is bounded to callers that enable the flag (the launcher passes false) and its consequence is performance, which the claim states; the trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review decide the formal outcome.\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-transconf.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_transconf_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{},\n \\\"candidate\\\":{\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The obligation and binding are supplied with the check so the claim exists before the plan references it; the duty is the documented transitive-conflict skipping under the flag the implementation provides.\\\",\\\"action\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"question\\\":q,\\\"obligation\\\":claim,\\\"bindings\\\":[b13]}}\nsub['sources']=srcs\njson.dump(plan,open('plan-transconf.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-transconf.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-transconf.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
